WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.053
A reviewer can ask: which requirement does this change

00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:03.541
implement?

00:00:03.924 --> 00:00:05.352
What inputs does it accept?

00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:07.082
What happens on failure?

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.777
Which tests changed?

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.587
Are secrets or private data exposed?

00:00:12.028 --> 00:00:13.677
Is there an obvious rollback?

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.649
Does the documentation still agree with the behavior?

00:00:17.252 --> 00:00:20.283
A small verified commit keeps these questions manageable.

00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:23.986
Avoid rerunning the same complete suite repeatedly when

00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:27.167
nothing relevant has changed, but do run checks again when

00:00:27.202 --> 00:00:30.082
a change or failure makes earlier results stale.
